@startuml domain-model
' TurbineH — Internal Invoicing & Payment Tracking System (Submission 2, task #42)
' Domain model: the main concepts of the problem domain, their attributes and
' associations, derived from the Functional Requirements and the 22 use cases.
' No types or operations: those belong to the class diagram (#45).

left to right direction
hide circle
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

skinparam class {
    BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    BorderColor #2B3E6A
    FontColor #000000
}
skinparam package {
    BorderColor #2B3E6A
    FontColor #2B3E6A
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FDE2B8
    BorderColor #2B3E6A
    FontColor #000000
}
skinparam arrow {
    Color #2B3E6A
}

package "Customers and subscriptions" {
    class Customer {
        tradingName
        legalName
        taxId
        taxAddress
        country
        workingCurrency
        status
        deleted
    }
    class Contact {
        name
        email
        phone
        contactRole
        whatsAppConsent
        preferredLanguage
        active
    }
    class Tag {
        name
    }
    class Subscription {
        startDate
        billingStartDate
        status
        agreedRate
        paymentTermDays
    }
    class Pause {
        reason
        startDate
        reactivationDate
    }
    class CommercialException {
        exceptionType
        value
        startDate
        endDate
    }
    class Cancellation {
        requestDate
        effectiveDate
        origin
    }
    class RateTier {
        minAnnualRevenue
        maxAnnualRevenue
        monthlyPrice
    }
    class AnnualReview {
        year
        annualRevenue
        revenueSource
        status
        effectiveDate
        previousPrice
        newPrice
    }
}

package "Invoicing" {
    class Invoice {
        invoiceType
        status
        number
        issueDate
        dueDate
        currency
        totalAmount
    }
    class InvoiceSeries {
        code
        lastNumber
    }
    class InvoiceLine {
        description
        quantity
        unitPrice
        discount
    }
    class Concept {
        name
        defaultPrice
    }
    class Tax {
        name
        rate
    }
    class InvoiceDocument {
        fileName
        generatedAt
    }
    class DeliveryAttempt {
        channel
        recipients
        sentAt
        result
    }
    class MessageTemplate {
        templateType
        language
        version
    }
}

package "Collections" {
    class PaymentTransaction {
        source
        amount
        currency
        transactionDate
        reference
    }
    class Reconciliation {
        reconciledAmount
        reconciledAt
        automatic
        reversed
        reversalReason
    }
    class Reminder {
        reminderType
        scheduledDate
        sentAt
    }
    class BillingIssue {
        issueType
        status
        priority
        resolution
    }
    class Comment {
        text
        restricted
        createdAt
    }
    class Attachment {
        documentType
        description
        fileName
    }
}

package "Users and governance" {
    class User {
        corporateEmail
        role
        active
    }
    class Delegation {
        startDate
        endDate
    }
    class ApprovalRequest {
        requestType
        reason
        status
        decisionComment
        decidedAt
    }
    class Notification {
        eventType
        priority
        read
        handled
    }
    class AuditEntry {
        action
        target
        occurredAt
    }
    class AccountingPeriod {
        startDate
        endDate
        status
    }
    class AutomationRun {
        job
        startedAt
        itemsProcessed
        failures
    }
    class Backup {
        createdAt
        status
    }
}

' --- Customers and subscriptions
Customer "1..*" -- "0..*" Contact : has
Customer "0..*" -- "0..*" Tag : labelled with
Customer "0..*" -- "1" User : responsible user
Customer "1" -- "0..*" Subscription : contracts
Subscription "1" -- "1..*" Concept : recurring concepts
Subscription "1" -- "0..*" Pause : paused by
Subscription "1" -- "0..*" CommercialException : adjusted by
Subscription "1" -- "0..1" Cancellation : ended by
Subscription "1" -- "0..*" AnnualReview : reviewed in
AnnualReview "0..*" -- "1" RateTier : proposes

' --- Invoicing
Customer "1" -- "0..*" Invoice : billed with
Subscription "0..1" -- "0..*" Invoice : generates
Invoice "0..*" -- "1" InvoiceSeries : numbered in
Invoice "1" *-- "1..*" InvoiceLine : contains
InvoiceLine "0..*" -- "0..1" Concept : based on
InvoiceLine "0..*" -- "1" Tax : taxed with
Invoice "1" *-- "0..1" InvoiceDocument : preserved as
Invoice "1" -- "0..*" DeliveryAttempt : sent through
DeliveryAttempt "0..*" -- "1" Contact : sent to
DeliveryAttempt "0..*" -- "1" MessageTemplate : uses
Invoice "0..1" -- "0..*" Invoice : corrected by

' --- Collections
PaymentTransaction "1" -- "0..*" Reconciliation : applied in
Reconciliation "0..*" -- "1" Invoice : settles
Invoice "1" -- "0..*" Reminder : followed up by
Customer "1" -- "0..*" BillingIssue : concerns
BillingIssue "0..*" -- "0..1" Invoice : about
BillingIssue "1" -- "0..*" Comment : discussed in
Customer "1" -- "0..*" Attachment : documents
Invoice "1" -- "0..*" Attachment : documents

' --- Users and governance
User "1" -- "0..*" Delegation : delegates
Delegation "0..*" -- "1" User : to
User "1" -- "0..*" ApprovalRequest : requests
ApprovalRequest "0..*" -- "0..1" User : decided by
ApprovalRequest "0..*" -- "0..1" Invoice : about
User "1" -- "0..*" Notification : receives
User "1" -- "0..*" AuditEntry : performs
Invoice "0..*" -- "1" AccountingPeriod : belongs to
AutomationRun "0..1" -- "0..*" Invoice : generates
Backup "0..*" -- "0..1" User : restored by

note bottom of Cancellation
  **FR4.1**: no new invoices from the
  effective date; previous invoices stay
  in collection (C4).
end note

note bottom of Reconciliation
  **FR3.1**: an invoice is paid only through
  the transactions that justify it; a
  reconciliation can be reversed.
end note

note bottom of AutomationRun
  Scheduled jobs (monthly generation,
  reminders, payment checks, backups)
  are system behaviour, not an actor
  (professor's answer, #27).
end note

@enduml
